  "title": "Noble Jump: Heli-Ops, Blackhawks and Dutch Army ",
  "description": "NATO’s new high readiness ‘spearhead’ force is being deployed for the first time, as Exercise NOBLE JUMP gets underway with forces converging in Zagan, Poland for simulated combat. Units assigned to the Very High Readiness Joint Task Force (VJTF) were given orders to deploy on Tuesday afternoon (9 June 2015), and will exercise until 19 June. Over 2,000 troops from nine NATO nations are participating in the exercise, which continues the process of testing and refining the force.\r\nUS Blackhawk helicopters transport Dutch soldiers into simulated hostile territory. Close-up video of soldiers running from helicopters and searching tents in a practice mission. Helmet camera video of Dutch soldiers bringing mock detainee onto helicopter. \r\n",
